   "text": "I bring the evening I actually have. Meet me among the ordinary sounds around me, the light beneath the door, and the things still out of place. I ask for a little room inside my thoughts to remember your presence. Help me receive this moment without demanding that it be perfect. For a moment, leave the list alone. Breathe naturally, without trying to reach a particular rhythm. Notice where you are supported. Let your next breath arrive in its own time, while this simple prayer settles: Shepherd, lead me into rest. He restoreth my soul: he leadeth me in the paths of righteousness for his name's sake.",
